  "notes": "{襲|おそ}う is a transitive godan verb meaning to attack, assault, or strike.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を for the target: Xを{襲|おそ}う\n\nUSAGE CONTEXTS:\n1. Physical attacks: {敵|てき}を{襲|おそ}う (attack the enemy)\n2. Natural disasters: {台風|たいふう}が{町|まち}を{襲|おそ}う (typhoon strikes the town)\n3. Emotions/feelings: {不安|ふあん}が{襲|おそ}う (anxiety strikes)\n\nPASSIVE FORM (COMMON):\n- Xに{襲|おそ}われる: to be attacked/struck by X\n- {眠気|ねむけ}に{襲|おそ}われる: to be overcome by drowsiness\n- {恐怖|きょうふ}に{襲|おそ}われる: to be seized by fear\n\nRELATED:\n- {襲撃|しゅうげき}: attack, raid (noun)\n- {奇襲|きしゅう}: surprise attack",
